# SeatLock — Movie Ticket Booking System

A production-oriented Movie Ticket Booking System built with **Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, Prisma, Redis, BullMQ and Stripe**.

The main engineering goal is **correctness under concurrency**: when multiple users try to book the same seat at the same time, the system must ensure that a seat cannot be successfully booked by two users.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Node.js |
| API | Express.js |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| ORM | Prisma |
| Cache / Lock | Redis |
| Distributed Locking | Redlock |
| Background Jobs | BullMQ |
| Payments | Stripe |
| Authentication | JWT + bcrypt |
| Validation | Zod |
| Logging | Pino |
| Testing | Jest + Supertest |
| Deployment | Docker / Docker Compose |

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Client[Client / Frontend] --> API[Express API]
    API --> Auth[JWT Auth]
    API --> Validation[Zod Validation]
    API --> RateLimit[Redis Token Bucket]
    API --> Booking[Booking Module]
    API --> Payment[Payment Module]
    API --> Cache[Cache-Aside]
    Booking --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
    Booking --> Redis[(Redis)]
    Payment --> DB
    Payment --> Stripe[Stripe]
    Stripe --> Webhook[Stripe Webhook]
    Webhook --> DB
    Webhook --> Saga[Saga / Confirmation]
    DB --> Outbox[Outbox Events]
    Outbox --> Queue[BullMQ]
    Queue --> Redis
    Redis --> Worker[Worker]
    Worker --> DB
    Worker --> Booking
```

Detailed system design is in **[ARCHITECTURE.md](./ARCHITECTURE.md)**.

