## Core Engineering Invariants

1. A `ShowSeat` cannot have more than one successful booking.
2. An expired held seat must eventually become available.
3. A Stripe webhook event must not be applied twice.
4. A repeated idempotency key must not create a second logical payment operation.
5. A committed critical state change must have its corresponding outbox event persisted in the same transaction.
6. Background jobs must re-check current database state before destructive actions.

